-- Equality of two random lists that both recurse over a runtime argument
-- has no probability variant (refused: "found no way to convert to IR in
-- probability mode"; generate only). With literal
-- lengths (coin 2 == coin 2) it compiles and answers 0.25. Found by
-- experiments_nest llm-noisy-channel-decoding (rung 3b: typo channel on the
-- writer's side, glyph reads on the reader's: `corrupt cs == perceive gs`).
-- Task random-list-equality-over-runtime-lists-no-probability.
coin xs = if isNull xs then [] else (if Uniform < 0.5 then 1 else 0) : coin (tail xs)
main xs ys = coin xs == coin ys
